cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, benchmark, or data, please cite both the
  conference paper (preferred-citation) and this repository.
title: >-
  Structured Domain Grounding for Natural-Language Querying of Japan's
  Large-Scale PM2.5 Knowledge Graph — Reproducibility Artifact
abstract: >-
  Camera-ready reproducibility artifact for the BDA 2026 paper. Contains the
  AirCypher-150 execution-validated NL-to-Cypher benchmark (150 items), the
  Domain Knowledge Base (DKB) for JPM2KG, the evaluation pipeline for six
  prompting configurations across four open-source LLMs and a fine-tuned
  Text2Cypher baseline, all 3,750 raw generation records, and the
  camera-ready result tables and statistics.
